=2 Walkthrough
* First you need to obtain a base weapon to be augmented. There's one weapon for each job:

|^Weapon|Job|Weapon|Job
|{p:Fay Crozier}|{p:Summoner}|{p:Erlking's Blade}|{p:Blue Mage}
|{p:Fay Staff}|{p:Scholar}|{p:Erlking's Sword}|{p:Paladin}
|{p:Fay Lance}|{p:Dragoon}|{p:Erlking's Tabar}|{p:Beastmaster}
|{p:Fay Gendawa}|{p:Ranger}|{p:Erlking's Kheten}|{p:Warrior |Warrior}
|{p:Fane Baselard}|{p:Thief}|{p:Oberon's Knuckles}|{p:Monk}
|{p:Fane Hexagun}|{p:Corsair}|{p:Rindomaru}|{p:Samurai}
|{p:Dweomer Knife}|{p:Bard}|{p:Oberon's Sainti}|{p:Puppetmaster}
|{p:Dweomer Scythe}|{p:Dark Knight}|{p:Tsukumo}|{p:Ninja}
|{p:Oberon's Rapier}|{p:Red Mage}|{p:Dweomer Maul}|{p:White Mage |White Mage}
|{p:Ogre Jambiya}|{p:Dancer}|{p:Ogre Sickle}|{p:Black Mage}

* Trade one of the weapons to {n:Callisto}, {z:Grauberg (S)} (F-6).
* Find any of the {n:Watchful Pixies|Watchful Pixie} located in one of the following Shadowreign zones and choose to begin the battle:

|^Pixie Location|Mobs
|{z:West Sarutabaruta (S)} (F-10)|1x Poroggo Gourmand, 6x Poroggo Toady
|{z:East Ronfaure (S)} (J-7)|Faytrapper Vashgash, Faygorger Ram x2, Faygorger Sheep x4
|{z:North Gustaberg (S)} (H-6)|Stabnix Skewerfinger, Pixie Impaler x10
|{z:Grauberg (S)} (J-11)|{m:Ru'Bha Stonewall}, {m:Sentinel Wivre} x4
|{z:Vunkerl Inlet (S)} (?)|Madthrasher Zradbodd, Almops, Edonus, Glacial Wisp x 4?
|{z:Batallia Downs (S)} (F-7)|Gnashfang Rahskhas, Rahskhas's Pet x4
|{z:Meriphataud Mountains (S)} (I-6)|{m:Yii Haqi the Threnodist} {m:Nuu Gazo the Dirgerimer} {m:Slate Scorpion} x2 {m:Ochre Scorpion} x2
|{z:Beaucedine Glacier (S)} (H-10)|Shesha, Kaliya, Vasuki, Astika
|{z:Xarcabard (S)} (J-8)|Megalotaur, Torvotaur

* Once the NM's are defeated, a {n:Jubilant Pixie} NPC will spawn. Speak to the Jubilant Pixie and the weapon you traded to {n:Callisto} will be offered to you with random augments.
** If you do not like the augments you can choose to refuse to take the weapon, up to five attempts to get better augments.

* Details for augment are only sparsely documented online, and appear to differ per weapon. [1][2][3]
** Notable possibilities include:
*** +magic skill, added effect elemental damage, added effect status effects, enmity modifiers, +WSD (up to 5%), Store TP, DA/TA, Subtle Blow, Primary Stats, Song Spellcasting Time, Cure Potency, and certain **Resist** modifiers (1-5%).
** Availability of various augment possibilities definitely depends on job, and also possibly on zone and other factors.
** (With the right mods this could be useful with gear sets especially if used in a less important weapon slot, but since TP will be reset to zero, it would have to be done intelligently. Most players should probably not bother with this content in current-day retail.)

